<title>USA: ErgoBilt Inc Q1 net income profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>ErgoBilt Inc Q1 net income profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pro Forma   Pro Forma</p>
<p>					  March 31, 1997 March 31, 1996</p>
<p> Sales						  $4,672     $3,582</p>
<p> Net Income						385	 (27)</p>
<p> Net Income Per Share				 0.06     (0.01)</p>
<p>Shares Outstanding (As if issued and</p>
<p>outstanding for all periods presented)</p>
<p>						     6,056,000  4,256,000</p>
<p>(Dollars In Thousands)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Company said it completed its acquisition of BodyBilt Seating on Feb 5, 1997, but first quarter 1997 pro forma results reflect the acquisition of BodyBilt by ErgoBilt as if it were completed on Jan 1, 1997.  Since the acquisition of BodyBilt occurred in the middle of the quarter, actual results will reflect ErgoBilt's performance for the entire first quarter and BodyBilt's performance for only two months. The company reported actual net income of $440,000, or $0.09 per share, from $3.7 million in revenues with 4.7 million shares outstanding.</p>
</text>
